+/// `f64`s that a team's phases read and write as plain slices, so a loop over them vectorizes
+/// as a loop over a `Vec` does.
+///
+/// Sound only under the team's phase discipline, which is why the accessors are `unsafe`:
+/// - a phase's items run only between [`Team::run`]'s publish (a release store of the phase
+///   ticket, acquired by every claim) and its return (after acquiring the completion count that
+///   every item released), so what the leader wrote before a phase is visible to its items, what
+///   they wrote is visible to the leader after it, and no item's slice outlives its phase;
+/// - within a phase, a cell that any item writes is written by that item alone, and read by no
+///   other item and not by the leader's `meanwhile`.
+///
+/// Every call site says which cells its phase writes and which it only reads.
+pub struct SharedF64s(Box<[UnsafeCell<f64>]>);
